1
00:00:06,632 --> 00:00:10,761
<i>We will introduce the survivor</i>
<i>of the exile zone's final match.</i>

2
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,346
-Of course.
-They must've played this morning.

3
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:13,639
The final one.

4
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:16,850
-Dong-jae?
-XITSUH?

5
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:23,440
2 HOURS EARLIER

6
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:28,153
Do we get right into it?

7
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:31,907
<i>We will now begin the final match.</i>

8
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:35,035
<i>Please make your way</i>
<i>to a spot of your choice.</i>

9
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:36,787
Let's go.

10
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:45,337
<i>The one and only winner of the final match</i>

11
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,256
<i>will return to the game area</i>

12
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:50,008
<i>and compete in </i>The Devil's Plan <i>once more.</i>

13
00:00:50,634 --> 00:00:52,761
<i>The final match of the exile zone is</i>

14
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:55,097
<i>Point Gomoku.</i>

15
00:00:56,348 --> 00:00:58,642
<i>Each round will consist of</i>

16
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:03,689
<i>selection, betting, and placement.</i>

17
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:07,859
<i>The player who has survived longer</i>
<i>in the exile zone</i>

18
00:01:07,943 --> 00:01:10,237
<i>will be the selection player for Round 1,</i>

19
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:14,658
<i>and from Round 2 onward,</i>
<i>the selection player will alternate.</i>

20
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:19,496
<i>The selection player will have 90 seconds</i>

21
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:23,292
<i>to choose three consecutive spots</i>
<i>and mark them on the monitor.</i>

22
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:24,459
Three spots?

23
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:30,173
<i>Each round, both players will be given</i>
<i>ten points each.</i>

24
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:33,510
<i>Both players will have 90 seconds</i>

25
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:37,681
<i>to distribute their given points</i>
<i>across the three selected spots.</i>

26
00:01:38,265 --> 00:01:42,185
<i>A minimum of one point</i>
<i>must be bet on each spot,</i>

27
00:01:42,269 --> 00:01:45,564
<i>and points can only be used</i>
<i>in whole numbers.</i>

28
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:48,108
<i>After betting,</i>
<i>only half of the remaining points</i>

29
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:50,402
<i>will be carried over to the next round,</i>

30
00:01:50,986 --> 00:01:53,572
<i>and any decimal will be dropped.</i>

31
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:57,284
<i>For example, in Round 1,</i>
<i>a player may choose to bet</i>

32
00:01:57,367 --> 00:02:02,831
<i>three points, one point, and one point</i>
<i>on the three spots, respectively.</i>

33
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:04,916
<i>Their five remaining points</i>
<i>will be halved,</i>

34
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,377
<i>and the decimal will be dropped,</i>

35
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:10,964
<i>leaving two points</i>
<i>to be carried over to the next round.</i>

36
00:02:11,048 --> 00:02:14,343
<i>In Round 2, 10 new points will be given,</i>

37
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:17,638
<i>bringing the total available to 12 points.</i>

38
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:22,100
<i>The stone of the player</i>
<i>who bet more points on each spot</i>

39
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:23,644
<i>will automatically be placed there.</i>

40
00:02:24,227 --> 00:02:28,982
<i>At this point, the points bet</i>
<i>and remaining points will not be revealed.</i>

41
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:34,321
<i>However, if both players bet</i>
<i>the same number of points on a spot,</i>

42
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:37,908
<i>the stone of the player</i>
<i>who did not select spots that round</i>

43
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:38,992
<i>will be placed there.</i>

44
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:46,375
<i>If a five-in-a-row is formed</i>
<i>after all three stones have been placed,</i>

45
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:49,878
<i>the player who formed it first wins.</i>

46
00:02:50,921 --> 00:02:54,174
<i>If multiple five-in-a-row lines</i>
<i>have been formed simultaneously,</i>

47
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:58,303
<i>the player with more lines wins.</i>

48
00:02:58,387 --> 00:03:02,391
<i>We will now begin the final match.</i>

49
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,603
<i>You take turns</i>
<i>to place three stones at a time,</i>

50
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:09,147
but they're not automatically yours.

51
00:03:09,231 --> 00:03:13,777
You have to bet your points
to claim each stone.

52
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,070
I realized this would involve

53
00:03:15,779 --> 00:03:17,280
a lot of strategic play.

54
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:20,367
<i>It was pretty interesting.</i>
<i>The spots are chosen in advance,</i>

55
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:22,953
but whoever bets higher
gets to claim them.

56
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,623
<i>Jung Won-young will play as black,</i>

57
00:03:26,706 --> 00:03:28,834
<i>and XITSUH will play as white.</i>

58
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:32,546
<i>Jung Won-young,</i>
<i>who has survived longer in the exile zone,</i>

59
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:34,756
<i>will select first.</i>

60
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,508
<i>Jung Won-young,</i>

61
00:03:36,591 --> 00:03:37,968
<i>please mark the spots</i>

62
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:40,303
<i>where you would like to</i>
<i>place your stones on the monitor.</i>

63
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:43,890
<i>I couldn't place three stones</i>
<i>just anywhere.</i>

64
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:46,685
<i>They had to be in a diagonal</i>
<i>or straight line,</i>

65
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:51,898
<i>so my plan was to build up</i>
<i>my attack routes one by one.</i>

66
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:03,243
<i>Please make your bids for each spot.</i>

67
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:11,168
<i>First, I had to distribute my points.</i>

68
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:16,840
<i>I figured taking that particular spot</i>
<i>would open up more attack routes.</i>

69
00:04:17,758 --> 00:04:19,676
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

70
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:23,597
<i>The remaining points</i>
<i>have been carried over,</i>

71
00:04:24,139 --> 00:04:26,725
<i>and ten new points have been added.</i>

72
00:04:27,309 --> 00:04:30,270
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

73
00:04:35,484 --> 00:04:37,194
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

74
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:44,743
<i>I wanted to take control</i>
<i>of whatever area I could early on,</i>

75
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:47,954
<i>so I bet points without reservation.</i>

76
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:55,295
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

77
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,756
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

78
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:00,967
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

79
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:09,726
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

80
00:05:20,237 --> 00:05:22,155
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

81
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:24,991
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

82
00:05:25,075 --> 00:05:26,701
<i>In most cases, no one won all three spots.</i>

83
00:05:26,785 --> 00:05:28,537
So I had to decide on my main battleground

84
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,831
and bet high on that spot
using the carried-over points

85
00:05:30,914 --> 00:05:32,165
<i>so he couldn't outbid me.</i>

86
00:05:32,249 --> 00:05:34,125
<i>That's how I kept count.</i>

87
00:05:34,626 --> 00:05:37,712
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

88
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:40,298
<i>When I was the selection player,</i>

89
00:05:40,382 --> 00:05:41,633
<i>I tried to pick spots</i>

90
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:44,844
<i>where I thought I'd still be safe</i>
<i>even if I lost all three.</i>

91
00:05:47,264 --> 00:05:49,140
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

92
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:52,519
Is he throwing away this turn?

93
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:05,657
I think he is.

94
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:09,536
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

95
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:11,997
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

96
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:15,208
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

97
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:23,466
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

98
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:28,096
<i>One spot was really critical,</i>

99
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:30,515
<i>while I could afford to</i>
<i>give up the others.</i>

100
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,900
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

101
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:47,240
<i>After I failed to secure any spots</i>
<i>with 1, 1, and 8 points,</i>

102
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:52,954
I realized XITSUH was also going all in
when defending important spots.

103
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:57,417
It felt like we both established
a baseline for effective attacks.

104
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,294
You had to bid nine or more for key spots.

105
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:02,631
<i>If both players</i>
<i>bet the same number of points on a spot,</i>

106
00:07:02,714 --> 00:07:06,176
<i>the non-selection player's stone</i>
<i>is placed there.</i>

107
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:09,554
<i>In other words, even if you have found</i>
<i>and selected a key spot,</i>

108
00:07:09,638 --> 00:07:12,682
<i>you can only place your stone there</i>

109
00:07:12,766 --> 00:07:14,893
<i>by outbidding your opponent.</i>

110
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:19,939
<i>The player who manages their points well</i>
<i>and secures the decisive placements</i>

111
00:07:20,023 --> 00:07:21,858
<i>will take the win in this game.</i>

112
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:25,111
I've lost out big time. Damn it.

113
00:07:26,613 --> 00:07:29,783
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

114
00:07:32,077 --> 00:07:34,412
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

115
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:43,004
<i>Five, four, three, two, one.</i>

116
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:47,550
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

117
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:49,844
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

118
00:07:49,928 --> 00:07:51,179
<i>It was so intense.</i>

119
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:55,225
<i>I had to calculate both my best move</i>
<i>and my opponent's before making a move,</i>

120
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:58,687
<i>while also predicting</i>
<i>our respective worst-case scenarios.</i>

121
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:03,274
<i>There were so many spots</i>
<i>where it was a 50-50 gamble.</i>

122
00:08:03,358 --> 00:08:06,152
<i>I suspect XITSUH</i>
<i>was feeling the exact same way.</i>

123
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:09,781
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

124
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,916
<i>-Please make your bids.</i>
<i>-</i>Would he have any left?

125
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:26,006
How many points is that? Four?

126
00:08:26,089 --> 00:08:27,048
This is nine.

127
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:31,011
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

128
00:08:31,094 --> 00:08:33,513
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

129
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:37,016
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

130
00:08:38,852 --> 00:08:40,687
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

131
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:43,189
He's aiming for that, huh?

132
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:54,367
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

133
00:08:54,451 --> 00:08:56,786
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

134
00:08:56,870 --> 00:09:00,331
I kept wondering
because the points weren't revealed.

135
00:09:00,415 --> 00:09:01,708
<i>I wasn't sure</i>

136
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:04,127
<i>whether we were both bluffing</i>
<i>or going all out in each round.</i>

137
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:07,714
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

138
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,096
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

139
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:21,436
All right, let's both use up everything.

140
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:28,860
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

141
00:09:29,611 --> 00:09:30,487
Well done.

142
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:34,991
That was a good move.

143
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:39,913
<i>If you select a spot that extends</i>
<i>beyond your opponent's five-in-a-row</i>

144
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:42,624
<i>and bet the minimum of one point,</i>

145
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:46,795
<i>your opponent's stone will be placed there</i>
<i>regardless of their bid.</i>

146
00:09:46,878 --> 00:09:50,089
<i>This results in a six-in-a-row or more,</i>
<i>like in the diagram,</i>

147
00:09:50,173 --> 00:09:53,218
<i>disrupting your opponent's attack plan.</i>

148
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:57,889
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

149
00:09:58,515 --> 00:10:00,558
<i>I selected three spots aggressively,</i>

150
00:10:00,642 --> 00:10:03,603
<i>looking for possible attack routes</i>
<i>near the six-in-a-row.</i>

151
00:10:04,229 --> 00:10:06,106
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

152
00:10:08,108 --> 00:10:10,401
If I use up nine points,
I'm left with four.

153
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:16,825
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

154
00:10:16,908 --> 00:10:19,410
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

155
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:21,788
He's too smart for such mind games.

156
00:10:22,413 --> 00:10:25,375
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

157
00:10:29,379 --> 00:10:31,297
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

158
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:32,966
<i>There were many turns</i>

159
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:37,804
<i>where Won-young seemed to be forcing me</i>
<i>to burn through all my points.</i>

160
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:40,265
Suppose I wanted to carry over 1 point
and bid 6, 1, and 1.

161
00:10:40,849 --> 00:10:43,768
But if Won-young bid 7, 2, and 2,

162
00:10:43,852 --> 00:10:44,853
it's game over for me.

163
00:10:44,936 --> 00:10:47,397
It was like he was saying, "Are you really
gonna save that one point?"

164
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:50,316
That sort of mind game
was very much in play.

165
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,360
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

166
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:54,487
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

167
00:10:54,571 --> 00:10:56,656
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

168
00:10:56,739 --> 00:10:58,992
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

169
00:10:59,701 --> 00:11:01,578
The whole board
will be filled at this rate.

170
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:04,205
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

171
00:11:04,289 --> 00:11:07,208
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

172
00:11:09,711 --> 00:11:11,629
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

173
00:11:12,255 --> 00:11:14,257
He could block it with eight.

174
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:16,176
<i>Every time I was placing my bids,</i>

175
00:11:16,259 --> 00:11:19,470
<i>I analyzed and verbally went over</i>
<i>what I'd do if I were XITSUH.</i>

176
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,139
Maybe 9, 3, and 1.

177
00:11:25,018 --> 00:11:26,811
Would I be able to win that with three?

178
00:11:36,863 --> 00:11:40,450
<i>I even tried spreading it out a bit</i>
<i>by betting 5, 5, and 1.</i>

179
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:42,660
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

180
00:11:42,744 --> 00:11:45,580
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

181
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:48,541
It evened out. Damn, that's too bad.

182
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:53,254
It's impossible to get a five-in-a-row
by taking all three spots in a turn.

183
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:54,797
To complete a five-in-a-row,

184
00:11:54,881 --> 00:11:56,507
you place three to an existing two,

185
00:11:56,591 --> 00:11:58,509
two to an existing three,

186
00:11:58,593 --> 00:12:00,053
or one to an existing four.

187
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,847
But placing three to an existing two
doesn't make sense.

188
00:12:02,931 --> 00:12:05,350
It's impossible to take all three at once.

189
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:07,268
Nobody's gonna just hand you all three.

190
00:12:07,352 --> 00:12:09,270
So is placing three
to an existing two possible?

191
00:12:09,354 --> 00:12:11,272
That's still 50-50.

192
00:12:11,898 --> 00:12:13,399
If I decide to block it,

193
00:12:13,483 --> 00:12:15,735
I can just go all in
on one of the two to do so.

194
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,445
So the smartest way

195
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:19,697
would be to secure one spot
next to an existing four,

196
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:23,618
but since both of us would go all in
to defend that one spot,

197
00:12:23,701 --> 00:12:26,704
I figured the most effective move

198
00:12:26,788 --> 00:12:31,459
was to have 14 or 15 points ready
and bet 1, 1, and the rest of my points.

199
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:33,044
So I devised a strategy

200
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:36,255
of saving up points
and landing one decisive blow.

201
00:12:36,339 --> 00:12:39,676
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

202
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:44,681
Placing three stones in a straight line
leads to a lot of dead space.

203
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:47,809
<i>If there are only two spaces</i>
<i>between stones,</i>

204
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:50,269
<i>you can't place on those spots.</i>

205
00:12:50,353 --> 00:12:52,855
<i>You'd have to use two turns to place</i>
<i>in those two spots</i>

206
00:12:52,939 --> 00:12:54,190
<i>or just give up entirely.</i>

207
00:12:54,273 --> 00:12:55,733
If you don't wanna be disrupted,

208
00:12:55,817 --> 00:12:58,194
the spots in the middle
aren't your best bet.

209
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:04,075
The corners and edges are actually harder
for your opponent to interfere with.

210
00:13:06,369 --> 00:13:08,705
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

211
00:13:08,788 --> 00:13:10,456
That's a great move.

212
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,459
He's going for that diagonal.

213
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:15,336
He gets to block this

214
00:13:16,421 --> 00:13:19,173
and aim for double five-in-a-row.

215
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:21,426
If I block it with 1, 4, and 5,

216
00:13:22,385 --> 00:13:24,137
I could secure at least one.

217
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:25,555
But if he's crazy enough to--

218
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:27,557
<i>Thirty seconds remaining.</i>

219
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,184
Would he assume I'd only use one here
and score it with two?

220
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:32,979
Would he be that insane?

221
00:13:34,397 --> 00:13:36,441
No, he's not that bad.

222
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:38,568
No, he has to be
since he made it this far.

223
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:41,529
Four.

224
00:13:48,036 --> 00:13:49,912
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

225
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:52,331
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

226
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:58,004
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

227
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:03,176
<i>There's no need to build</i>
<i>on the chain for defense.</i>

228
00:14:03,259 --> 00:14:07,430
<i>You could just force your opponent</i>
<i>to place their stone on the sixth spot.</i>

229
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:13,352
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

230
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:20,943
<i>He marked three spots</i>
<i>all the way at the far right edge.</i>

231
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:24,447
That's when I realized
he was utilizing the same strategy.

232
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:27,825
I didn't want any, but I knew
he meant for me to get them all.

233
00:14:27,909 --> 00:14:29,786
Dial 112 to call the police.

234
00:14:34,165 --> 00:14:36,209
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

235
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:38,920
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

236
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:41,422
This is tough.

237
00:14:41,506 --> 00:14:43,132
He keeps blocking everything.

238
00:14:43,758 --> 00:14:46,886
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

239
00:14:50,098 --> 00:14:52,225
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

240
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,643
He's also saving his points, huh?

241
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:57,105
<i>I bid one point on all three spots</i>
<i>to carry over as many points as possible.</i>

242
00:14:57,814 --> 00:14:59,649
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

243
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:02,860
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

244
00:15:04,946 --> 00:15:06,197
He'll probably place there.

245
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,281
Let's go for it.

246
00:15:09,075 --> 00:15:11,160
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

247
00:15:11,786 --> 00:15:14,622
You get the priority.
I'm not taking those.

248
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:16,791
Mind games, huh?

249
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:20,461
It's either seven and seven
or six and eight.

250
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:24,507
It's definitely a mind game.

251
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:26,175
<i>When your opponent makes an attack,</i>

252
00:15:26,259 --> 00:15:29,011
<i>you can't tell</i>
<i>if it's a real one or a feint.</i>

253
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:33,391
They might just bet one for all three
because they think you're gonna defend.

254
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,560
<i>Ten seconds remaining.</i>

255
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:42,024
<i>But still, I tried to invest my points</i>
<i>into my defense when I could.</i>

256
00:15:42,108 --> 00:15:46,737
<i>Five, four, three, two, one.</i>

257
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:50,450
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

258
00:15:50,533 --> 00:15:53,077
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

259
00:15:53,161 --> 00:15:56,706
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

260
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:03,087
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

261
00:16:04,755 --> 00:16:06,299
I could lose.

262
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:13,598
Maybe I shouldn't have gone all in.

263
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:18,102
I'll score this.

264
00:16:21,022 --> 00:16:22,940
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

265
00:16:23,024 --> 00:16:25,568
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

266
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:27,278
<i>Ten seconds remaining.</i>

267
00:16:29,614 --> 00:16:31,324
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

268
00:16:31,949 --> 00:16:34,702
I feel like we might have
the same number of points left.

269
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:37,830
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

270
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,502
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

271
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,879
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

272
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:48,674
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

273
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:56,557
<i>Five, four, three, two, one.</i>

274
00:16:57,934 --> 00:16:59,644
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

275
00:17:00,228 --> 00:17:02,897
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

276
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:03,940
Two here…

277
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:06,442
The bottom two spots are defense,
and the top is the attack.

278
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:08,986
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

279
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:15,451
<i>Five, four, three, two, one.</i>

280
00:17:16,661 --> 00:17:18,371
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

281
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:20,706
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

282
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:22,458
This is so hard.

283
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:26,837
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

284
00:17:28,172 --> 00:17:30,174
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

285
00:17:31,259 --> 00:17:32,885
Is he trying to make me take them?

286
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:35,888
<i>There were a lot of black stones nearby,</i>

287
00:17:35,972 --> 00:17:37,848
<i>so I decided to take at least one there.</i>

288
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:40,017
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

289
00:17:41,102 --> 00:17:43,437
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

290
00:17:43,521 --> 00:17:46,399
Even after I bid 8, 1, and 1?

291
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:50,403
I bid eight points on the spot
next to the four-in-a-row,

292
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:52,530
but all three spots got taken
by the black stones.

293
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:55,074
That's weird.

294
00:17:56,075 --> 00:17:58,828
<i>I kept running mind games</i>
<i>one after another,</i>

295
00:17:58,911 --> 00:18:00,913
but he somehow had enough points
to take them all.

296
00:18:00,997 --> 00:18:02,873
That made something clear for me.

297
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:06,294
He used up his carried-over points.

298
00:18:06,377 --> 00:18:08,713
That reset my counting.

299
00:18:10,673 --> 00:18:11,841
What do I do?

300
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:13,718
A black line had formed.

301
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:18,014
I thought I could create
multiple attack routes

302
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:20,516
if I used this space
strategically later on.

303
00:18:21,017 --> 00:18:24,270
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

304
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:27,023
By this point, I was planning to
save as many points as possible

305
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:31,444
so that I could land a decisive blow
to end the game.

306
00:18:31,527 --> 00:18:36,032
<i>Five, four, three, two, one.</i>

307
00:18:37,450 --> 00:18:39,285
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

308
00:18:40,036 --> 00:18:42,663
So you're taking a break
to save some points? Okay.

309
00:18:42,747 --> 00:18:44,498
<i>As the game went on</i>
<i>and stones accumulated,</i>

310
00:18:44,582 --> 00:18:46,167
I felt the moment was approaching

311
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:49,754
where whoever could bet
just one more point on that one stone

312
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:52,757
next to a four-in-a-row
or a gap would take it.

313
00:18:53,341 --> 00:18:54,300
You can have them.

314
00:18:58,220 --> 00:18:59,972
Let's be conservative for now.

315
00:19:01,724 --> 00:19:03,559
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

316
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:06,479
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

317
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:09,273
<i>XITSUH, please mark your spots.</i>

318
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:12,652
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

319
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:15,988
He's defending from the back, huh?

320
00:19:16,947 --> 00:19:19,075
Damn it, that was a good move.

321
00:19:24,205 --> 00:19:25,247
Have it your way.

322
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:28,000
My time will come.

323
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:31,462
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

324
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:34,173
<i>Ten new points have been added.</i>

325
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:36,008
XITSUH saved a lot of points too.

326
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:39,136
The next turn is gonna be huge.

327
00:19:39,762 --> 00:19:42,723
<i>Jung Won-young, please mark your spots.</i>

328
00:19:42,807 --> 00:19:44,058
Fifteen is the max.

329
00:19:46,977 --> 00:19:48,604
This isn't looking good.

330
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:50,648
Why not, right?

331
00:19:55,778 --> 00:19:57,613
<i>Please make your bids.</i>

332
00:20:09,083 --> 00:20:10,459
One on these two.

333
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:12,837
Do I go all in on the other one?

334
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:15,506
<i>I couldn't decide if I should use up</i>
<i>everything and go for 13, 1, and 1,</i>

335
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:18,926
or save a little and go for 11, 1, and 1.

336
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:20,469
I was torn.

337
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:22,930
<i>But I didn't think</i>
<i>Won-young would go all in just then</i>

338
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:25,266
<i>because there was</i>
<i>a better spot for him to attack.</i>

339
00:20:25,349 --> 00:20:28,436
He'd be better off attacking just below
that seven-in-a-row on the middle left.

340
00:20:28,519 --> 00:20:30,312
That's where you can
really go on the offensive.

341
00:20:30,396 --> 00:20:32,857
If he just placed stones there,
he'd get two three-in-a-row formations

342
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:34,358
and a four-in-a-row.

343
00:20:34,442 --> 00:20:35,484
So I knew

344
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:41,323
I had to defend if I didn't wanna lose,
but it could also be a mind game.

345
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:51,959
<i>Letting it drag on</i>
<i>when I could land a decisive blow</i>

346
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:53,753
<i>felt like an unnecessary risk.</i>

347
00:20:54,587 --> 00:20:59,091
<i>Five, four, three, two, one.</i>

348
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:00,176
<i>So I went all in.</i>

349
00:21:01,844 --> 00:21:03,471
<i>The stones have been placed.</i>

350
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:06,390
It's over.

351
00:21:07,141 --> 00:21:09,268
<i>Jung Won-young has won.</i>

352
00:21:09,852 --> 00:21:12,104
<i>That concludes the final match.</i>

353
00:21:12,188 --> 00:21:14,565
<i>Farewell, XITSUH.</i>

354
00:21:15,858 --> 00:21:16,942
I had a great time.

355
00:21:17,026 --> 00:21:18,027
Good game.

356
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:25,785
<i>I was able to take part</i>
<i>in the final match of the exile zone</i>

357
00:21:25,868 --> 00:21:28,329
because I stayed focused and survived.

358
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:31,624
I didn't think I'd be the one
to go out in it though.

359
00:21:41,634 --> 00:21:42,843
I gave it my all.

360
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:44,637
I can say that with certainty.

361
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,931
<i>I've been almost ruthless toward myself.</i>

362
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:48,891
<i>Even when I felt exhausted,</i>

363
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:52,436
<i>I never stopped pushing myself,</i>
<i>telling myself,</i>

364
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,188
<i>"Just one more game."</i>

365
00:21:54,271 --> 00:21:57,399
<i>I took it one day at a time like that</i>
<i>and made it all the way here.</i>

366
00:21:57,483 --> 00:22:00,152
There were so many twists and turns,
and honestly, it was so much fun.

367
00:22:00,236 --> 00:22:04,031
The one thing I promised myself
before coming onto <i>The Devil's Plan</i>

368
00:22:04,698 --> 00:22:05,950
was to do things my way.

369
00:22:06,534 --> 00:22:08,869
No backstabbing for a tiny advantage.

370
00:22:10,079 --> 00:22:11,914
Rather than betraying trust
for a little gain,

371
00:22:12,581 --> 00:22:14,792
I chose to believe in my own abilities,
accept risks,

372
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:18,671
and step up to lead when I can.

373
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:22,383
That was how I survived,

374
00:22:22,466 --> 00:22:25,094
and I feel like
I've proven something to myself.

375
00:22:29,557 --> 00:22:31,183
<i>Before we begin the game,</i>

376
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:33,978
<i>-we will introduce the survivor</i>
-I knew it.

377
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:35,729
-Of course.
<i>-of the exile zone's final match.</i>

378
00:22:35,813 --> 00:22:37,189
-They must've played this morning.
-The final one.

379
00:22:40,109 --> 00:22:41,527
-Dong-jae?
-XITSUH?

380
00:22:46,115 --> 00:22:46,991
What?

381
00:22:51,787 --> 00:22:52,788
Man, that's impressive.

382
00:22:52,871 --> 00:22:53,831
-Thank you.
-Seriously.

383
00:22:57,835 --> 00:22:59,044
-Well done.
-Look at you.

384
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:00,921
-Welcome.
-You made it to the living area.

385
00:23:01,005 --> 00:23:03,048
-Welcome back.
-What matches did you play?

386
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:05,342
I sent Dong-jae home in a memory game,

387
00:23:05,426 --> 00:23:07,136
Yurisa in an arithmetic game,

388
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:08,846
and XITSUH in an abstract strategy game.

389
00:23:11,432 --> 00:23:13,559
-Amazing.
-His confidence is through the roof.

390
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:15,978
You should've come.
I wanted to practice for the finals.

391
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:23,777
It's not easy to pick yourself back up
after a breakdown.

392
00:23:23,861 --> 00:23:26,739
<i>I'm amazed he's managed it and returned.</i>

393
00:23:26,822 --> 00:23:29,658
<i>The exile zone is no walk in the park.</i>

394
00:23:29,742 --> 00:23:31,910
<i>I can't believe</i>
<i>he beat so many fierce competitors.</i>

395
00:23:31,994 --> 00:23:34,371
He must be completely fired up today.

396
00:23:34,455 --> 00:23:36,832
I felt he'd be the one
to look out for today.

397
00:23:37,791 --> 00:23:41,879
<i>Here is the current Piece count</i>
<i>for each player.</i>

398
00:23:45,007 --> 00:23:48,510
<i>Jung Won-young,</i>
<i>please return to the game area.</i>

399
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:52,765
What? Am I getting ten Pieces?

400
00:23:52,848 --> 00:23:54,850
I hope so. Let's see.

401
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:56,560
Five?

402
00:23:57,227 --> 00:24:01,523
<i>Currently, Jang Dong-min</i>
<i>holds the most Pieces.</i>

403
00:24:01,607 --> 00:24:02,900
Did he get some from the others?

404
00:24:04,818 --> 00:24:07,529
<i>Now, let me introduce</i>
<i>the sixth main match.</i>

405
00:24:08,030 --> 00:24:09,573
<i>Today's main match is</i>

406
00:24:09,657 --> 00:24:11,492
<i>HIT, STAY.</i>

407
00:24:11,575 --> 00:24:15,162
<i>In HIT, STAY, players must survive</i>

408
00:24:15,245 --> 00:24:18,499
<i>by managing the sum of their number cards</i>
<i>to win betting chips.</i>

409
00:24:18,582 --> 00:24:19,917
Yes. Chips!

410
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:22,836
<i>Before the game begins,</i>
<i>lottery balls will be drawn</i>

411
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:24,838
<i>to determine the first player.</i>

412
00:24:24,922 --> 00:24:27,508
<i>The game will proceed clockwise,</i>

413
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:28,926
<i>and from the next round onward,</i>

414
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:31,720
<i>the player to the left</i>
<i>of the previous first player</i>

415
00:24:31,804 --> 00:24:34,014
<i>will become the new first player.</i>

416
00:24:34,515 --> 00:24:37,559
<i>In HIT, STAY,</i>
<i>the following cards will be used.</i>

417
00:24:37,643 --> 00:24:39,311
<i>One seven card, two six cards,</i>

418
00:24:39,395 --> 00:24:41,021
<i>three five cards,</i>

419
00:24:41,105 --> 00:24:42,564
<i>four four cards,</i>

420
00:24:42,648 --> 00:24:43,982
<i>five three cards,</i>

421
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:45,984
<i>six two cards,</i>

422
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:48,153
<i>seven one cards,</i>

423
00:24:48,237 --> 00:24:51,740
<i>and seven minus-one cards.</i>

424
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:57,329
<i>Each player will be given 30 chips</i>
<i>to start,</i>

425
00:24:57,413 --> 00:25:00,457
<i>and all Pieces</i>
<i>currently in players' possession</i>

426
00:25:00,541 --> 00:25:02,000
<i>will be exchanged for chips.</i>

427
00:25:02,626 --> 00:25:05,754
<i>Each Piece exchanges for one chip.</i>

428
00:25:06,547 --> 00:25:07,631
<i>When the game begins,</i>

429
00:25:07,715 --> 00:25:10,426
<i>players will submit one chip each</i>
<i>as the base bet,</i>

430
00:25:10,509 --> 00:25:12,553
<i>and the base bet will increase</i>

431
00:25:12,636 --> 00:25:15,556
<i>by one chip every ten rounds.</i>

432
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:20,519
<i>After the base bet,</i>
<i>the dealer will roll an eight-sided die</i>

433
00:25:20,602 --> 00:25:22,730
<i>numbered 5 through 12.</i>

434
00:25:22,813 --> 00:25:27,067
<i>The number that comes up</i>
<i>will be the limit number for that round.</i>

435
00:25:27,151 --> 00:25:28,527
-What?
-"Limit number."

436
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:29,862
<i>-Players must then</i>
-"Limit number"?

437
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:34,450
<i>manage their number cards so that the sum</i>
<i>does not exceed the limit number.</i>

438
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:38,954
-That's fun.
<i>-Once the limit number is set,</i>

439
00:25:39,037 --> 00:25:41,165
<i>the dealer will shuffle the number cards</i>

440
00:25:41,248 --> 00:25:44,626
<i>and deal three cards face down</i>
<i>to each player.</i>

441
00:25:45,335 --> 00:25:48,464
<i>Each player will then select one card,</i>

442
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:50,674
<i>which will be revealed to all players.</i>

443
00:25:50,758 --> 00:25:52,801
<i>Once all cards have been revealed,</i>

444
00:25:52,885 --> 00:25:55,721
<i>the first player will initiate</i>
<i>the first round of betting.</i>

445
00:25:56,305 --> 00:25:57,931
<i>Players may choose one of the following.</i>

446
00:25:58,015 --> 00:26:01,018
<i>Call, raise, or fold.</i>

447
00:26:01,101 --> 00:26:04,062
<i>The maximum number of chips</i>
<i>that can be bet</i>

448
00:26:04,146 --> 00:26:08,609
<i>cannot exceed the chip count</i>
<i>of the player with the fewest chips.</i>

449
00:26:09,109 --> 00:26:12,404
<i>Once all players have bet</i>
<i>the same number of chips,</i>

450
00:26:12,488 --> 00:26:14,615
<i>the first round of betting will end.</i>

451
00:26:15,491 --> 00:26:17,743
<i>Players who bet in the first round</i>

452
00:26:17,826 --> 00:26:20,746
<i>may each receive</i>
<i>one additional card in turn,</i>

453
00:26:20,829 --> 00:26:22,664
<i>starting from the first player.</i>

454
00:26:23,165 --> 00:26:25,334
<i>To receive an additional card,</i>
<i>players must choose "hit."</i>

455
00:26:25,417 --> 00:26:29,546
<i>To receive no more cards,</i>
<i>players must choose "stay."</i>

456
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:33,050
<i>Additional cards</i>
<i>will be revealed to all players.</i>

457
00:26:33,133 --> 00:26:34,718
Okay, so they're made public.

458
00:26:34,802 --> 00:26:37,095
<i>This process will be repeated</i>

459
00:26:37,179 --> 00:26:40,098
<i>until all additional cards are exhausted,</i>

460
00:26:40,182 --> 00:26:42,392
<i>or all players choose "stay."</i>

461
00:26:42,476 --> 00:26:46,438
<i>Once additional cards have been dealt,</i>
<i>the second round of betting will begin.</i>

462
00:26:46,522 --> 00:26:48,315
<i>Once the second round of betting ends,</i>

463
00:26:48,398 --> 00:26:53,445
<i>all participating players</i>
<i>will reveal their cards and compete.</i>

464
00:26:54,071 --> 00:26:57,616
<i>Any player whose card total</i>
<i>exceeds the limit number</i>

465
00:26:57,699 --> 00:26:59,701
<i>will finish last in that round.</i>

466
00:27:01,787 --> 00:27:04,164
<i>Among the players whose card total</i>
<i>did not exceed the limit,</i>

467
00:27:04,248 --> 00:27:07,376
<i>the player with the higher card total</i>
<i>will win</i>

468
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:09,878
<i>and take all the chips in the pot.</i>

469
00:27:10,963 --> 00:27:13,131
<i>If the card totals are equal,</i>

470
00:27:13,215 --> 00:27:16,426
<i>the player with more cards will win.</i>

471
00:27:17,135 --> 00:27:20,013
<i>If both the card totals</i>
<i>and the number of cards held are the same,</i>

472
00:27:20,097 --> 00:27:23,433
<i>or if all players' card totals</i>
<i>have exceeded the limit number,</i>

473
00:27:23,517 --> 00:27:27,896
<i>the round will be considered a tie,</i>
<i>and the bet chips will be split equally.</i>

474
00:27:28,564 --> 00:27:30,691
<i>Any remaining chips</i>
<i>will be taken in order,</i>

475
00:27:30,774 --> 00:27:32,276
<i>starting with the first player.</i>

476
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:34,152
Free chips.

477
00:27:34,236 --> 00:27:36,947
<i>The first player to lose all their chips</i>

478
00:27:37,030 --> 00:27:41,076
<i>will become the lowest-ranked player</i>
<i>and be eliminated from</i> The Devil's Plan.

479
00:27:41,743 --> 00:27:43,287
<i>As the game continues,</i>

480
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:46,748
<i>players will go to prison</i>
<i>in the order they run out of chips.</i>

481
00:27:47,416 --> 00:27:49,960
<i>The last remaining player</i>

482
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:52,921
<i>will advance to the finals.</i>

483
00:27:53,005 --> 00:27:54,882
-That's how? Okay.
-Last man standing?

484
00:27:54,965 --> 00:27:56,341
-Until it's one-on-one.
-The last one standing.

485
00:27:56,425 --> 00:27:57,843
Until only one person remains.

486
00:27:57,926 --> 00:28:00,304
I figure aggressive betting
won't be an issue

487
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:05,726
because of the rule that the first person
to run out of chips gets eliminated.

488
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:09,104
I felt like I was at a disadvantage
because I had no Piece yesterday,

489
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:11,815
but I think I can expect
better results today.

490
00:28:12,399 --> 00:28:15,777
Ultimately, it comes down to matching
the limit number as closely as possible.

491
00:28:16,361 --> 00:28:17,779
You just have to
send someone packing first.

492
00:28:17,863 --> 00:28:21,658
For now, hitting that limit
is the most important task at hand.

493
00:28:21,742 --> 00:28:26,246
I think I need to play defensively
early on to avoid elimination.

494
00:28:26,330 --> 00:28:28,248
Wait, what if they form alliances again?

495
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:32,461
It's not easy playing
with two skilled liars.

496
00:28:33,337 --> 00:28:34,504
You're all gathered here.

497
00:28:34,588 --> 00:28:36,214
-Yeah.
-We're just doing our own thing.

498
00:28:36,298 --> 00:28:38,842
I was hoping to get you eliminated,
but I don't think there's a way.

499
00:28:38,926 --> 00:28:40,844
-No wonder I felt this strange chill.
-There's coffee.

500
00:28:41,845 --> 00:28:43,805
-So they just gave you five Pieces?
-Yeah, as a reward.

501
00:28:43,889 --> 00:28:45,641
-Damn.
-She got the reward for the hidden stage.

502
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:47,768
-If I hadn't won yesterday--
-Her challenge was much harder.

503
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:49,519
So noisy.

504
00:28:50,229 --> 00:28:51,730
I wish I could send Dong-min home.

505
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:54,566
With more than a 50% chance,

506
00:28:55,567 --> 00:28:57,361
I can take up to two.

507
00:28:58,237 --> 00:29:01,323
Out of the total 35 cards, 20 are good.

508
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:05,243
<i>In other words,</i>
<i>more than half the cards are good.</i>

509
00:29:05,327 --> 00:29:08,330
So there's no reason to be afraid

510
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:11,083
<i>of choosing "hit"</i>
<i>and taking additional cards.</i>

511
00:29:11,166 --> 00:29:12,626
<i>Your time is up.</i>

512
00:29:12,709 --> 00:29:15,087
<i>Everyone, please gather in the hall.</i>

513
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:16,213
Let's go!

514
00:29:16,296 --> 00:29:18,548
<i>We will now begin HIT, STAY.</i>

515
00:29:18,632 --> 00:29:22,886
<i>We will first draw lottery balls</i>
<i>to determine the order.</i>

516
00:29:23,512 --> 00:29:25,555
The first player is seated
to the dealer's left.

517
00:29:25,639 --> 00:29:27,557
-One, two, three, four.
-Thank you.

518
00:29:27,641 --> 00:29:29,393
This could be the order of elimination.

519
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:32,688
-How nice. Should we stick to this?
-Maybe.

520
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:34,439
Please sit in order.

521
00:29:35,274 --> 00:29:37,150
<i>You are the top five,</i>

522
00:29:37,234 --> 00:29:40,362
<i>about to play the final main match</i>
<i>before the finals.</i>

523
00:29:41,488 --> 00:29:45,742
<i>On the first day, in Either Or,</i>
<i>you revealed a part of your personality</i>

524
00:29:45,826 --> 00:29:48,870
<i>through a series of choices.</i>

525
00:29:48,954 --> 00:29:53,583
<i>Four of you chose</i>
<i>the performance bonus with confidence,</i>

526
00:29:53,667 --> 00:29:57,462
<i>and one chose</i>
<i>the insurance payout for stability.</i>

527
00:29:58,046 --> 00:30:00,173
<i>JAE JAE, John Park,</i>

528
00:30:00,257 --> 00:30:02,134
<i>and Jung Won-young</i>
<i>chose to play as a team,</i>

529
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:06,888
<i>while Jang Dong-min and Hyun Kyung-lyul</i>
<i>chose to play alone.</i>

530
00:30:07,431 --> 00:30:12,269
<i>The most heated debate was over</i>
<i>greater good versus personal gain,</i>

531
00:30:12,352 --> 00:30:16,231
<i>with an even split</i>
<i>of eight players on each side.</i>

532
00:30:16,315 --> 00:30:19,693
<i>Those who chose greater good,</i>

533
00:30:19,776 --> 00:30:23,196
<i>John Park, JAE JAE, and Jung Won-young,</i>
<i>are currently players in prison,</i>

534
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:25,157
<i>while those who chose personal gain,</i>

535
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:29,911
<i>Jang Dong-min and Hyun Kyung-lyul,</i>
<i>are currently players in the living area.</i>

536
00:30:29,995 --> 00:30:32,247
<i>The fierce competitive spirit of then</i>
<i>is mirrored today in this match.</i>

537
00:30:32,331 --> 00:30:35,042
<i>You have used every opportunity available</i>

538
00:30:35,125 --> 00:30:36,668
<i>to increase the prize money</i>
<i>to 500 million won,</i>

539
00:30:36,752 --> 00:30:39,921
<i>accumulating 200 million won so far.</i>

540
00:30:40,005 --> 00:30:42,841
-Those selfish people.
-That's abysmal.

541
00:30:42,924 --> 00:30:47,095
<i>We will now give you</i>
<i>one more choice to make.</i>

542
00:30:48,096 --> 00:30:49,723
-What?
<i>-There will be a bonus prize</i>

543
00:30:49,806 --> 00:30:51,099
<i>of 100 million won on the line.</i>

544
00:30:52,559 --> 00:30:53,894
GREATER GOOD / PERSONAL GAIN

545
00:30:53,977 --> 00:30:54,811
What the?

546
00:30:54,895 --> 00:30:58,565
<i>If three or more players</i>
<i>choose greater good,</i>

547
00:30:58,648 --> 00:31:01,234
<i>one hundred million won</i>
<i>will be added to the prize money.</i>

548
00:31:01,318 --> 00:31:02,277
That's amazing.

549
00:31:02,361 --> 00:31:05,614
<i>On the other hand,</i>
<i>if a player chooses personal gain,</i>

550
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:09,493
<i>they will receive ten chips.</i>

551
00:31:10,911 --> 00:31:13,830
-We've been screwed over once.
<i>-The devices will now be handed out.</i>

552
00:31:13,914 --> 00:31:15,957
-Damn it.
-Either Or again?

553
00:31:16,458 --> 00:31:19,419
-All right.
-Stop messing around already.

554
00:31:20,087 --> 00:31:21,630
Who didn't vote for it last time?

555
00:31:21,713 --> 00:31:22,631
These two.

556
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:23,757
You two, go first.

557
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:28,220
If you guys go first, the three of us…

558
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:29,846
-We'll follow suit.
-We will.

559
00:31:29,930 --> 00:31:31,473
-But you need to show us first.
-Right.

560
00:31:31,556 --> 00:31:36,061
The last time, we chose greater good first
and got screwed over big time.

561
00:31:36,144 --> 00:31:39,356
If even one of you doesn't show us
your choice…

562
00:31:39,439 --> 00:31:40,357
Both of you must show us.

563
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:43,360
Right, if you don't,
we'll go for personal gain.

564
00:31:43,443 --> 00:31:44,528
-That's right.
-All right.

565
00:31:44,611 --> 00:31:47,447
It makes sense to add to the prize money
if you think you can win.

566
00:31:47,531 --> 00:31:51,243
But after we vote,
and one of the three screws us over…

567
00:31:51,326 --> 00:31:53,453
-We'd never.
-I mean, it's a possibility.

568
00:31:53,537 --> 00:31:55,205
-We only need three votes.
-Sure, it's possible.

569
00:31:55,288 --> 00:31:57,082
-All it takes is three votes.
-Possible?

570
00:31:57,165 --> 00:31:58,416
If you make us lock in first

571
00:31:58,500 --> 00:32:00,585
and one of you betrays us,
that'd be a massive blow.

572
00:32:00,669 --> 00:32:03,588
-Up to the third person who locks in…
-We've been through this before.

573
00:32:03,672 --> 00:32:05,674
-There's no need to walk us through it.
-Right.

574
00:32:05,757 --> 00:32:07,008
-We get it.
-Of course.

575
00:32:07,092 --> 00:32:10,011
I definitely wanna add to the prize money.

576
00:32:10,095 --> 00:32:12,013
I can choose greater good,

577
00:32:12,097 --> 00:32:16,226
but that becomes pointless
if just one person chooses personal gain.

578
00:32:16,309 --> 00:32:17,394
That's undeniable.

579
00:32:17,477 --> 00:32:19,146
Then personal gain is the way to go,

580
00:32:19,229 --> 00:32:21,982
-and that changes everything for the game.
-Right.

581
00:32:22,065 --> 00:32:24,317
Nobody seems to care
about the prize money.

582
00:32:24,401 --> 00:32:25,360
It's not that.

583
00:32:25,443 --> 00:32:27,988
-We're torn because we <i>do</i> care.
-Right.

584
00:32:28,071 --> 00:32:29,281
So for the sake of survival?

585
00:32:29,364 --> 00:32:31,032
You need to win to see that money.

586
00:32:31,116 --> 00:32:33,702
-Either way, we all have a 20% chance
-Right.

587
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:35,287
-of winning right now.
-Correct.

588
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:40,750
So whether the prize is 200 million
or 300 million is up to us to decide.

589
00:32:40,834 --> 00:32:42,544
Let's just all go for personal gain.

590
00:32:43,503 --> 00:32:44,671
Then everyone would be at ease.

591
00:32:44,754 --> 00:32:46,548
But that doesn't change anything.

592
00:32:46,631 --> 00:32:49,259
We'll just be starting
with ten extra chips.

593
00:32:49,342 --> 00:32:50,260
What good would that do?

594
00:32:50,343 --> 00:32:51,595
It wouldn't be exactly the same.

595
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:54,222
It would be if all five of us
started with ten extra.

596
00:32:54,306 --> 00:32:57,100
-The game will just go on longer.
-It'd narrow the gap.

597
00:32:57,184 --> 00:32:59,394
-The baseline goes up from 30 to 40.
-Right.

598
00:32:59,478 --> 00:33:00,729
The ratio will change.

599
00:33:00,812 --> 00:33:02,481
-So in terms of ratios,
-Exactly. Ratio-wise…

600
00:33:02,564 --> 00:33:04,816
there's a difference
between 30 to 8 and 40 to 8.

601
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:06,651
-So--
-If everyone chooses greater good,

602
00:33:06,735 --> 00:33:09,404
I'm ever so slightly at a disadvantage.

603
00:33:09,488 --> 00:33:10,739
But I won't decide based on that.

604
00:33:10,822 --> 00:33:15,118
The most important player
in all of this is you, Kyung-lyul.

605
00:33:15,202 --> 00:33:16,411
-The choice is yours.
-Okay.

606
00:33:16,495 --> 00:33:17,954
Let's say you're set on personal gain

607
00:33:18,038 --> 00:33:20,415
-regardless of the situation.
-Right.

608
00:33:20,499 --> 00:33:22,000
-Then…
-We'll make the same choice.

609
00:33:22,083 --> 00:33:24,169
-We'll all choose that too.
-That's what I'm saying right now.

610
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:26,588
-Right, but--
-I have no choice but to go for it.

611
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:27,631
-I'm being honest.
-Okay.

612
00:33:27,714 --> 00:33:29,007
So you're fine with the pot as is?

613
00:33:29,090 --> 00:33:30,217
Yeah.

614
00:33:30,300 --> 00:33:31,968
Okay, personal gain it is then.

615
00:33:33,053 --> 00:33:34,179
Personal gain?

616
00:33:36,223 --> 00:33:37,057
Sure.

617
00:33:38,016 --> 00:33:38,850
Too bad.

618
00:33:39,351 --> 00:33:40,185
Yeah.

619
00:33:40,685 --> 00:33:42,771
-I don't wanna lie about my choice.
-All done?

620
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:43,897
Did you press it?

621
00:33:43,980 --> 00:33:44,814
Not yet.

622
00:33:45,398 --> 00:33:47,442
-But…
-It's a survival game. It can't be helped.

623
00:33:47,526 --> 00:33:50,862
I hope you can understand
that I don't have much of a choice.

624
00:33:50,946 --> 00:33:52,239
Of course.

625
00:33:52,822 --> 00:33:56,785
<i>Since three or more players</i>
<i>did not choose greater good,</i>

626
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:59,162
<i>the prize token cannot be obtained.</i>

627
00:33:59,246 --> 00:34:00,080
Damn it!

628
00:34:00,163 --> 00:34:04,876
<i>Jang Dong-min, Hyun Kyung-lyul, John Park,</i>

629
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:07,212
<i>JAE JAE, and Jung Won-young</i>

630
00:34:07,796 --> 00:34:10,757
<i>have chosen personal gain</i>
<i>and will each receive ten chips.</i>

631
00:34:11,341 --> 00:34:13,843
Your Pieces
will now be exchanged for chips.

632
00:34:13,927 --> 00:34:16,096
-Sure.
-I should've spent less yesterday.

633
00:34:16,805 --> 00:34:18,098
I really should've.

634
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:19,432
I had ten yesterday.

635
00:34:19,516 --> 00:34:20,600
JOHN PARK: 44 CHIPS

636
00:34:20,684 --> 00:34:21,559
Thank you.

637
00:34:22,227 --> 00:34:23,478
I have four Pieces.

638
00:34:23,561 --> 00:34:24,854
JAE JAE: 44 CHIPS

639
00:34:25,522 --> 00:34:26,940
-Exchanging eight Pieces.
-Lucky number.

640
00:34:27,023 --> 00:34:28,650
JANG DONG-MIN: 48 CHIPS

641
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:30,277
Round 1 will now begin.

642
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:32,404
The first player for Round 1
is Jung Won-young.

643
00:34:32,988 --> 00:34:34,406
Please place your base bets.

644
00:34:37,409 --> 00:34:38,868
I will now roll for the limit number.

645
00:34:41,663 --> 00:34:42,998
-The limit number is eight.
-Eight.

646
00:34:49,963 --> 00:34:51,381
I will now deal the cards.

647
00:35:06,896 --> 00:35:09,274
Please submit one card
face down to be revealed.

648
00:35:12,193 --> 00:35:13,737
Submissions are now complete.

649
00:35:13,820 --> 00:35:15,405
Please reveal your cards.

650
00:35:20,827 --> 00:35:22,454
We will now begin
the first round of betting.

651
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:25,373
Jung Won-young, as the first player,
please place your bet.

652
00:35:28,877 --> 00:35:29,878
I'll bet three.

653
00:35:29,961 --> 00:35:31,212
Jung Won-young has bet three chips.

654
00:35:31,838 --> 00:35:32,881
Hyun Kyung-lyul.

655
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:34,007
I'll fold.

656
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:35,133
I'll fold.

657
00:35:35,216 --> 00:35:36,176
Fold.

658
00:35:36,259 --> 00:35:37,385
JAE JAE.

659
00:35:38,303 --> 00:35:39,346
I'll call.

660
00:35:40,055 --> 00:35:41,806
-JAE JAE has called three chips.
-Yes.

661
00:35:41,890 --> 00:35:42,849
Jang Dong-min.

662
00:35:58,281 --> 00:35:59,532
I'll raise it by seven.

663
00:36:00,700 --> 00:36:02,786
Jang Dong-min has raised by seven
on top of three.

664
00:36:02,869 --> 00:36:03,912
Jung Won-young.

665
00:36:08,041 --> 00:36:09,250
How many chips do you have?

666
00:36:09,334 --> 00:36:10,585
Three more than you.

667
00:36:17,592 --> 00:36:18,968
I'll raise it by 37.

668
00:36:19,844 --> 00:36:21,137
Raise.

669
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:24,974
What's wrong with him?

670
00:36:25,684 --> 00:36:27,143
Are they both set to go?

671
00:36:27,227 --> 00:36:29,813
Darn it, I should've folded earlier.
I'll fold.

672
00:36:30,397 --> 00:36:31,314
Jang Dong-min.

673
00:36:35,777 --> 00:36:37,445
One will win, and the other will go home.

674
00:36:37,529 --> 00:36:39,155
Can't win now with that chip gap.

675
00:36:46,996 --> 00:36:48,415
I'll go all in.

676
00:36:48,498 --> 00:36:49,332
All in.

